meta {
  name: Remove Manager From Truck
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

delete {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/trucks/{{truckId}}/managers/{{truckManagerUserId}}
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{accessToken}}
}

docs {
  Removes one manager from a truck's manager set; the user itself is kept
  (`TruckResource.removeManagerFromTruck`, `common/controller/TruckResource.java:805`, service
  `TruckService.removeManagerFromTruck` → `unassignManagerFromTruck`). Roles: VAHN_ADMIN,
  TORG_ADMIN, FUND_MANAGER. Non-VAHN_ADMIN callers can only touch trucks owned by their own torg.
  Replaces the deprecated `PUT /api/trucks/{truckId}/unassign-manager?userId=`.

  Set `truckId`, `truckManagerUserId` (and `accessToken`) in the selected environment before
  each run.

  200 with the updated TruckDTO. If the removed manager was primary, the oldest remaining manager
  is promoted; if none remain the truck's manager is cleared. An in-progress trip managed by the
  removed user moves to the new primary manager, or to the torg admin when no manager is left.
  A user who is not a manager of the truck also gets 200 with the truck unchanged.

  404 "Vehicle not found with ID: ..." if the truck doesn't exist. 400 if the truck belongs to
  another torg.
}
